  "review_notes": [
    "mallon joined to kalon on the single comparative word 'better' (rule 39's test), replacing this verse's earlier reading that left mallon unrepresented. The cross-verse contrast is what decides it: the ASV writes 'better' where mallon stands and 'good ... rather than' at 9.43, 9.45 and 9.47 where it does not, so the comparative degree of 'better' is what mallon licenses.",
    "Both articles of the ton mikron touton ton pisteuonton phrase empty, the demonstrative taking the determiner slot and the participle the relativizer (rules 31, 38)."
  ]
